<title>UK: BA deal with American may fail-paper.</title>
<headline>BA deal with American may fail-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways' planned merger with American Airlines could face further delays and ultimately be scuppered by both the British government and the European Commission, the Guardian said on Friday.</p>
<p>The paper quoted a senior European Commissioner as saying BA had failed so far to convince Brussels or Britain's Office of Fair Trading that it could meet the tough competition criteria.</p>
<p>The Guardian said it understood the OFT was demanding BA give up six percent of its landing slots at Heathrow Airport but BA had offered only four percent.</p>
